{"format":"tvf-scene","v":1,"name":"example · three parties","loop":56,"ease":"inout","hold":0,"gravity":1,"wind":0,"trail":null,"camera":[{"t":0,"box":[-0.7444224,-0.0752103325,-0.546612083,0.107756193]},{"t":0.16,"box":[-0.7444224,-0.0752103325,-0.546612083,0.107756193]},{"t":0.19,"box":[-0.477186207,-0.0429206934,-0.329710345,0.0909341391]},{"t":0.5,"box":[-0.477186207,-0.0429206934,-0.329710345,0.0909341391]},{"t":0.53,"box":[-0.238344828,-0.0645517241,-0.0906206897,0.0831724138]},{"t":0.67,"box":[-0.238344828,-0.0645517241,-0.0906206897,0.0831724138]},{"t":0.7,"box":[-0.0263793103,-0.0729310345,0.290172414,0.113275862]},{"t":0.84,"box":[-0.0263793103,-0.0729310345,0.290172414,0.113275862]},{"t":0.87,"box":[0.331882759,-0.0715655172,0.632048276,0.082737931]}],"stops":[0.16,0.33,0.5,0.67,0.84],"beats":[{"title":"Standing in a corner","text":"Stand in the corner of a room: one wall runs off [to the left, one to the right, and up is the corner](#lit:0). A direction is the three together, [h : v : v₂], how much of each against the others, and no distance. None is negative, so a writer draws the directions as [one octant](#lit:1,2).\n\nA [ray](#lit:3) has to be cut somewhere to be drawn. Cut where its length is 1 and it lands on the octant; cut [where the three add to 1](#lit:4) and the octant flattens into a triangle, the writer's drawing that needs no standpoint."},{"title":"The triple corner","text":"Face on, the [triangle](#lit:5,10) holds every way three breadths can share a whole. The reader has one length, its thumb, two thumbs crossed and both the same H, so it gives every party that length: [the centre](#lit:12), (⅓, ⅓, ⅓), the triple corner, where every pair is at its own corner at once.\n\nThe truth lies [off it](#lit:13,14), here at (2/9, 2/3, 1/9), by two ratios no reading carries: how many thumbs the second party is, and the third. Amounts brought in move the reader's amounts toward it; nothing is redrawn."},{"title":"A sixth, a half, a third","text":"Swept evenly by area, the directions fall into [six orderings](#lit:6,7,8), a sixth each. [Each pair's corner](#lit:11) is a median of the triangle, and every pair has its median there, as in the plane.\n\nOne thing is new. [Near in everything](#lit:9), h the largest of the three, is exactly a third of the directions. Past the corner in one reading is a third, past in both a third."},{"title":"By area, not by angle","text":"\"Every direction alike\" has to be said carefully in space. On [Lambert's map](#lit:16,17), azimuth across and height up, equal area is equal room, and [v ≤ h](#lit:15) is half of it, under [its corner](#lit:19,20,21).\n\nSweep the two angles evenly and the [rings of altitude](#lit:18) crowd toward the vertical: v ≤ h falls to 0.343 and the near field to 0.233. Sweep evenly in height, Archimedes' hat-box, and they space out: a half, and a third."},{"title":"The heat about the look","text":"What the reader has is not the wedge but a heat map about its look. On a flat screen [rings holding a sixth of the directions each](#lit:22) stretch without end, the heat thinning as [cos³ of the angle off the look](#lit:27,25), [half at 37.5°](#lit:28).\n\nLaid so equal shares take equal room, the same rings pack under [the rim](#lit:24) at √2: the far field is not stretched but packed, and the heat turns with the look, centred on [whatever is looked at](#lit:23)."},{"title":"More parties, any size","text":"Nothing needed exactly two other parties. With n of them every pair keeps its corner, and near in everything is [1/(n + 1)](#lit:29,30,31,32,33): a half, a third, a quarter.\n\nAnd none of it needs a size. A [sphere](#lit:36) at the middle of a [cube](#lit:35) sends each direction to one point of its face, [at every size of cube](#lit:37); the direction is the same, the amount e times it. A reader holding the directions has the cube up to scale. [The essay](https://github.com/reportbase/wander/blob/main/papers/essays/05-three-parties.md)"}],"path":null,"items":[{"fill":{"color":"#f4f1ea","opacity":1},"stroke":null,"width":0,"open":false,"exact":{"x":[-0.9,0.9,0.9,-0.9],"y":[0.294827586,0.294827586,-0.294827586,-0.294827586],"r":null,"smooth":null,"ctrl":null,"holes":[]}},{"morph":0},{"morph":1},{"morph":2},{"morph":3},{"morph":4},{"morph":5},{"morph":10},{"morph":6},{"morph":7},{"morph":8},{"morph":9},{"morph":11},{"morph":12},{"morph":13},{"morph":14},{"morph":16},{"morph":15},{"morph":17},{"morph":18},{"morph":19},{"morph":20},{"morph":21},{"morph":22},{"morph":24},{"morph":23},{"morph":26},{"morph":25},{"morph":27},{"morph":28},{"morph":29},{"morph":30},{"morph":31},{"morph":32},{"morph":33},{"morph":34},{"morph":35},{"morph":36},{"morph":37},{"morph":38},{"morph":39},{"morph":40},{"morph":42},{"morph":41},{"morph":43},{"morph":44},{"morph":45},{"morph":46}],"morphs":[{"exact":true,"open":true,"holes":null,"keys":[{"x":[-0.722786897,-0.645517241,-0.645517241,-0.645517241,-0.568247586],"y":[-0.0477155172,-0.00310344828,0.0861206897,-0.00310344828,-0.0477155172],"r":[0,0,0,0,0],"c":[null,null,null,null,null]}],"fill":null,"inPlace":true,"lag":0,"fx":null,"own":{"parent":-1,"parentAt":null,"follow":null,"look":-1,"lookRef":0,"phase":0,"rate":1,"spin":0,"motion":null,"onto":null,"laps":1,"start":null,"times":null,"clip":{"start":0.004,"len":0.986,"show":"","in":{"kind":"draw","len":0.015}},"eases":null,"straight":false,"trail":null,"cols":null,"path":null},"stroke":"#3b4256","width":2,"strokeOpacity":1},{"exact":true,"open":false,"holes":null,"keys":[{"x":[-0.707334828,-0.70720138,-0.706804139,-0.706146207,-0.705227587,-0.704054481,-0.702626898,-0.700957241,-0.699051724,-0.69691655,-0.694557932,-0.691994481,-0.689229312,-0.686274828,-0.683149653,-0.679860001,-0.676424482,-0.672858623,-0.669174826,-0.66538862,-0.661515513,-0.657577237,-0.653586207,-0.649561034,-0.645517241,-0.641473449,-0.637448276,-0.633457246,-0.629518969,-0.625645862,-0.621859652,-0.61817586,-0.614610001,-0.611174482,-0.607884825,-0.604759659,-0.6018